+	// PUPIL = mask INTERSECT iris. The mask (white when none is bound) is sampled at the pupil's
+	// bounding scale (vDofBokehMask.y), the polygon at its own radius; their product is the
+	// physical aperture at every f-number. Stopping the iris down through the mask clips the
+	// silhouette corner by corner and rounds it off progressively - the two apertures are two
